
======================================================================================================
ROUTE D -- ADVERSARIAL NO-GO HUNT: CAN A LOCALLY-DRAGGED PASSIVE FRAME SUPPLY THE SPEED?
======================================================================================================
  a0 = c H_Lambda / Z, Z = sqrt(32 pi/3) = 5.78881 -> a0 = 9.3600e-11 m/s^2
  (canonical rho_DE footing); equivalently a0 = (c/2) sqrt(G rho_Lambda) = EXACTLY HALF the
  free-fall acceleration at the dark-energy density. kappa = 1/2 is Carl Zimmerman's and is
  absent from the prior literature. CAVEAT: 32pi/3 is the Einstein-coupling conversion
  factor and CANCELS in that reduction, so the content is the ONE number kappa, and it is
  FITTED, not derived. Alternate footing carried throughout: a0 = 1.1300e-10 m/s^2.
  Kernel in force: alpha = 2, mu(x) = x/sqrt(1+x^2). Retired: alpha = 1.

