======================================================================================================
VERDICT -- RANKED, WITH WHAT DIED
======================================================================================================
  THE OBSTRUCTION, IN ONE SENTENCE. Solar-system ranging forces the dragged frame to carry
  at most 1/25 of the vorticity of the matter that drags it, which kills a
  co-moving frame outright; the only construction that meets that cap for free is a
  potential flow, which is exactly blind to a stationary galaxy's rotation; and a potential
  flow's remaining translational drag fraction is pinned by a trace identity to be
  PROPORTIONAL TO THE LOCAL DENSITY, so one coupling cannot capture the bulk motion of a
  3.4-dex range of hosts -- 84% of real SPARC
  galaxies are left at >90% the cosmic frame, which the framework's own RAR excludes at
  4.6x. That is a closed loop built from three computed identities, not from rhetoric.

  RANKING (best first), with the assigned candidate numbers in brackets:
   1. [4] THE FRAME-VORTICITY BOUND -- RIGOROUS, and the sharpest single number here.
        delta a_pair = -w x curl u EXACTLY (symbolic; the symmetric part of grad u cancels
        identically, so ONLY vorticity is observable; negative control u = const passes).
        => rotational drag fraction g <= 4.02e-02 conservative / 1.39e-03 optimistic,
        i.e. 25x-717x below the MW's MEASURED Oort
        vorticity A-B = 8.815e-16 1/s. FOOTING-FREE. This alone excludes any
        frame that co-rotates with local matter, and it forces R_drag >= 22-131 kpc.
   2. [1 + 6] THE POTENTIAL-FLOW TRACE IDENTITY -- RIGOROUS, and it is the actual no-go.
        (a) FOR the framework: div(rho v) = -d rho/dt == 0 for any stationary system, so a
            potential-flow frame is EXACTLY rotation-blind, g = 0 identically. It is the
            one candidate that meets #1 for free. Reported at full strength.
        (b) AGAINST it: the surviving translational drag has f_ij = -kappa_d d_i d_j chi
            with Laplacian chi = rho, hence (1/3)Tr f = kappa_d rho(x)/3 POINTWISE, for any
            profile. So f is proportional to LOCAL DENSITY over 3.4 dex of
            real SPARC. Median-tuned: 4.12 dex residual = 18x budget with BOTH signs.
            Max-tuned (never over-drags, most generous): 0.93 dex = 4.2x, and
            84% of the sample collapses to f < 0.1 = the cosmic
            frame. a0_eff(rho_local) is the door the corpus nulled at 10.5 sigma.
   3. [2] LOCAL-COMOVING COLLAPSE -- RIGOROUS, corroborating: the RAR's own HI tracer IS the
        local matter, so lam = sigma_gas/Vflat on 135 real SPARC galaxies gives
        1.4-1.6 dex of a0 (7.2x budget), and at lam = 0 the closure has NO
        SOLUTION at all. Plus a 20% stars-vs-gas tracer split against a
        few-per-cent observed agreement. Same horn as #1 kills, different observable.
   4. [5] NESTING -- RIGOROUS as an ILL-DEFINEDNESS, NOT as a bound violation. a0_eff spans
        3.14 dex across nested systems; one u cannot serve the Sun's galactic
        orbit and the Earth's solar orbit (mismatch exactly 7.82). On alpha=2 the planets
        stay SAFE at 3e-7 of the Earth bound, so I do NOT sell this as a kill. It does
        force gamma_v = 1.000002 for wide binaries -- outside the FROZEN band --
        and re-specifies Front B's apex by 131 deg. Reported, not amended.
   5. [1 partial] SINGLE-SCALE SMOOTHING SQUEEZE -- *** PARTIAL: DOES NOT CLOSE. *** At the
        conservative vorticity-forced R_drag = 22 kpc, ZERO of 135
        SPARC galaxies fail host-domination against the cosmic mean, and an isolated field
        galaxy's residual spread is only 0.074 dex = 0.33x budget -- INSIDE it.
        It closes only for group members (4.9x)
        and on the optimistic leg (22/135 fail, spread 0.73-1.67 dex).
        A universal smoothed frame therefore SURVIVES this test for isolated massive hosts.
        It still costs a FIFTH CONSTANT. This is the horn I most wanted and did not get.
   6. [3] LORENTZ / SME -- DID NOT CLOSE. No killing bound derived. What is real: a dragged
        frame RE-SPECIFIES the frozen s^TX prediction (131 deg apex change,
        0.63x speed), so Front B needs re-derivation; and PPN preferred-frame parameters
        assume a spatially UNIFORM frame, so the corpus's alpha_2^MI ~ 1e-13 does NOT cover
        the gradient effect -- which is exactly why #1 had to be derived from scratch.
   7. [6] PASSIVITY -- *** DIED. *** I tried hard to prove that matter-dragging reinstates
        Einstein-aether strong coupling. It does not: the velocity Hessian is
        2(c1-c4)delta_ij, so c1 = c4 gives ZERO propagating modes WITH spatial gradients
        intact. Passivity is compatible with an elliptic drag operator. Its residue is real
        but indirect: ellipticity forces a boundary condition, which is the hypothesis #2
        needs. The brief guessed this would be the sharpest; it is the one that failed.

  SO: WHAT SURVIVES OF THE DOOR? Stated plainly, because 'four of six' is not 'six of six'.
  A locally-dragged passive frame is NOT ruled out in general. What IS ruled out is every
  prescription I could construct that is (a) built from the matter distribution, (b) passive,
  and (c) governed by one universal constant. The gap I could not shut is a
  gravitomagnetic-type VECTOR drag with a smoothing length ~1e2 kpc, applied to isolated
  massive hosts only. That is a narrow corner, it needs a fifth constant, its GR-natural
  coupling is ~1e-6 of the required size, and it inherits #4's nesting ill-definedness -- but
  it is not closed, and I will not say it is.

  NOVELTY, ASSESSED NOT ASSERTED. Nothing here is a new physical idea. Inertia relative to
  local matter is Mach; Sciama 1953 is the standard citation; the objection that a
  non-rigidly-dragged frame produces observable fictitious forces is classical, and #1 is
  its quantitative form on 2020s ephemerides. Milgrom 1994 owns the modified-inertia class
  and the orbit-dependence; Milgrom 2022 owns the single-frequency restriction. The
  gravitomagnetic vector-Poisson drag is Lense-Thirring. What appears to be NEW is narrow
  and internal: (a) the exact statement that the pair-differential anomaly is -w x curl u,
  which isolates the frame VORTICITY as the only observable of grad u and thereby turns a
  vague 'fictitious forces' worry into one clean number; (b) the trace identity pinning the
  potential-flow drag fraction to the LOCAL DENSITY pointwise, which routes this door into a
  door the corpus already closed; (c) the stationarity theorem in this context. All three
  are corollaries of textbook identities applied to this framework's own action.

  WHAT WOULD BE NEEDED TO FINISH / TO ESCAPE. Named, not hidden:
   * A drag that is NOT a potential flow and NOT co-rotating: a gravitomagnetic-type vector
     Poisson equation is the natural candidate and it evades #2 (it has vorticity by
     construction) -- but it must then satisfy #1's 25x vorticity
     suppression, which is what forces R_drag into #4's squeeze. Computing that coupling's
     actual amplitude (in GR it is O((v/c)^2), ~1e-6 of what is needed) is the open task.
   * Dispersion-supported systems have ZERO matter vorticity, so #1 says nothing about
     dwarf spheroidals or cluster galaxies. A real scope limit, stated not buried.
   * The vorticity bound needs a proper precession-residual treatment. I EXPECTED that to
     be TIGHTER than the ranging inversion. The one independent number I could compute (the
     LLR geodetic-precession residual) came out 29x LOOSER, so I DEMOTED my own headline
     from 717x to 25x and used 25x everywhere downstream. A dedicated ephemeris fit of a
     uniform frame rotation is the correct computation and it is NOT done here.
   * If the frame were sourced by the framework's own dark (AeST/ghost-condensate Q) sector
     rather than by baryons, #2's continuity argument would need redoing for that
     sector's own flux. Not attempted here. That is the least-closed corner.

  NOT CLAIMED: that a0 is derived (kappa = 1/2 is fitted); that the off-circular law is
  settled; that any live front is decided; that the theory is closed. Nothing here revives
  the TOE / Standard-Model claims retracted publicly on 2026-06-23.
